2026-08-16T11:59:59Z    [HD:Net sales] GATE critic: The +4.86% YoY growth you apply is inconsistent with Home Depot’s reported figures. If FY2025 Q2 net sales were $45.3bn (45,300 USDm), a +4.86% change implies FY2024 Q2 net sales of about 43,180 USDm. Home Depot’s Q2 FY2024 filing reports net sales materially higher than that (around $43.8bn), implying only ~+3.4% YoY. Using the correct YoY basis would reduce the FY2026 Q2 estimate to roughly 46,840 USDm, not 47,502 USDm.
2026-08-16T12:00:01Z    [DE:Worldwide net sales and revenues] GATE critic: Your growth input for FY2024Q3→FY2025Q3 is on the wrong basis. Deere explicitly reported that Worldwide net sales and revenues for Q3 2025 decreased 9% YoY to $12.018 billion, but you used −8.6% in the median. That mismatch implies you pulled the −8.6% from a different metric (likely Equipment Operations net sales) or period. Using inconsistent bases contaminates the median (−12.69%). On the correct basis (−16.8% and −9.0%), the median would be −12.9%, yielding ~USD 10,468m, not 10,492.5m.
2026-08-16T12:00:14Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: You’ve copied the FY2024Q3 fully diluted EPS of $6.29 into FY2026Q3. That is the wrong fiscal period: the cited source supports $6.29 for FY2024Q3, not FY2026Q3, and carrying a two-years-prior actual forward as a FY2026Q3 GAAP EPS estimate is not valid.
