2026-08-16T12:00:55Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Internal consistency error: you state the FY2026Q2 forecast applies 0.00% YoY growth (“anchor left unadjusted”) to FY2025Q2 adjusted diluted EPS of $4.68, which should yield exactly $4.68. The proposed value is $4.68001, implying a non‑zero growth and introducing unjustified five‑decimal precision. If growth is 0.00%, the forecast must be $4.68 exactly.
2026-08-16T12:01:10Z    [ADI:Revenue] GATE critic: Your primary input is “guidance_anchor+signal 3934.12,” but the only cited source for FY2026Q3 says “we are forecasting revenue of $3.9 billion, +/- $100 million.” There’s no documentary support for a 3,934.12 USDm anchor; that adds an unsupported +$34.12m and over‑precision relative to the stated guidance. On this basis you should anchor at 3,900 USDm (midpoint) or remain within the ±$100m band without inventing extra precision, so the 3,899.36 USDm result is built on the wrong basis.
